<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<cfsSimulation xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
               xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation ../../../../../share/xml/CFS-Simulation/CFS.xsd"
               xmlns="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation">

  <documentation>
    <title>Augmented Lagrange (Uzawa) contact: penetration driven to zero at a moderate penalty</title>
    <authors><author>kroppert</author></authors>
    <date>2026-08-06</date>
    <keywords><keyword>contact</keyword></keywords>
    <references>none</references>
    <isVerified>yes</isVerified>
    <description>
      The ContactPartialLiftoff3d model -- two stacked cubes under a pressure linear in x, p =
      1e6*(1 + 2*x), so the load carries a moment and the windward half of the interface opens
      -- with the single attribute formulation="augmentedLagrange" added.

      The partial-liftoff model is used deliberately rather than the plain patch test: its
      contact traction genuinely depends on the deformation, so the Uzawa loop has to ITERATE
      (seven outer iterations here) instead of converging in one step on a problem whose contact
      force is fixed by equilibrium alone.

      Against the penalty reference at the SAME normalPenalty="100", the penetration falls from
      1.06e-6 to 4.55e-15 while maxPressure, the resultant and the active set are unchanged: the
      penetration is removed by the multiplier rather than by the stiffness, so the tangent
      stays the positive definite penalty matrix it was. gapSequence records the penetration per
      outer iteration.

      integrationOrder is 6 for the same reason as in ContactPartialLiftoff3d: at the default
      order the two points that stay closed lie on one line and the upper body can rotate about
      it freely.
    </description>
  </documentation>

  <fileFormats>
    <input>
      <hdf5 fileName="ContactAugmentedLagrange3d.h5" linearizeEntities="__none__"/>
    </input>
    <output><hdf5/></output>
    <materialData file="mat.xml" format="xml"/>
  </fileFormats>

  <domain geometryType="3d">
    <regionList>
      <region name="master_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
      <region name="slave_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
    </regionList>
    <surfRegionList>
      <surfRegion name="master_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="slave_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="top"/>
      <surfRegion name="bottom"/>
    </surfRegionList>
  </domain>

  <fePolynomialList>
    <Lagrange><gridOrder/></Lagrange>
  </fePolynomialList>

  <integrationSchemeList>
    <scheme>
      <method>Gauss</method>
      <order>4</order>
      <mode>absolute</mode>
    </scheme>
  </integrationSchemeList>

  <sequenceStep>
    <analysis><static/></analysis>

    <pdeList>
      <mechanic subType="3d">
        <regionList>
          <region name="master_elem"/>
          <region name="slave_elem"/>
        </regionList>

        <contactList>
          <contactPair name="aug_contact"
                       primarySurface="master_iface"
                       secondarySurface="slave_iface"
                       slidingType="small"
                       formulation="augmentedLagrange"
                       normalPenalty="100"
                       initialGapHandling="fromMesh"
                       integrationOrder="6">
            <augmentation maxIter="20" tol="1e-8"/>
          </contactPair>
        </contactList>

        <bcsAndLoads>
          <!-- lower body fully supported -->
          <fix name="bottom">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/><comp dof="z"/>
          </fix>
          <!-- upper body: suppress the lateral rigid-body modes only. Its z support comes
               exclusively from the contact interface, which is the point of the test. -->
          <fix name="top">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/>
          </fix>
          <!-- linear in x: net force 1e6*4 plus a moment, so part of the interface opens -->
          <pressure name="top" value="1e6*(1+2*x)"/>
        </bcsAndLoads>

        <storeResults>
          <nodeResult type="mechDisplacement"><allRegions/></nodeResult>
        </storeResults>
      </mechanic>
    </pdeList>

    <linearSystems>
      <system>
        <solutionStrategy>
          <standard>
            <setup idbcHandling="penalty"/>
            <matrix storage="sparseNonSym" reordering="noReordering"/>
            <nonLinear method="newton" logging="no">
              <lineSearch type="none"/>
              <incStopCrit>1e-9</incStopCrit>
              <resStopCrit>1e-9</resStopCrit>
              <maxNumIters>20</maxNumIters>
            </nonLinear>
          </standard>
        </solutionStrategy>
        <solverList><directLU/></solverList>
      </system>
    </linearSystems>

  </sequenceStep>
</cfsSimulation>
